# This module's Go sources are LF in the index and must be LF in the worktree
# too. gofmt compares the bytes ON DISK, so a CRLF checkout makes `gofmt -l`
# list a file that is byte-identical to a clean one. Measured here on
# providers.go: gofmt listed it, the file had CRLF endings, and CI on Linux
# passed green — a false positive that costs a diagnosis every time it fires.
# eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf=true, which is what put the CRLF there.
*.go text eol=lf

# The vendored CLI is tracked with Git LFS. git cannot delta-compress a 20 MB
# binary between versions, so every vendoring added another full copy to the
# history permanently. Measured on 2026-09-20: 18 distinct blobs, and the
# packed repository at 55 MiB after gc.
#
# LFS stores a ~130 byte pointer in the commit and keeps the binary outside the
# object database, so a clone fetches the current version instead of all
# eighteen.
#
# -text is explicit rather than left to content sniffing: the file has no
# extension, and a single converted byte would corrupt the ELF silently.
#
# This stops future growth only. The eighteen blobs already in the history stay
# where they are: removing them means rewriting history, which invalidates every
# existing clone and every commit hash. That is a separate decision.
#
# Anyone checking out this repository needs git-lfs installed. CI already checks
# out with lfs: true.
bin/clinical-trials-pp-cli-linux filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text